{
 "_doc": "Next-step chains (assistant/scripts/tracking/chains.py; TRACKING_DESIGN.md ruling 4). A chain is a list of gates an entity must pass in order; each gate has a due offset (days from the chain's anchor date, or a window from the previous gate) and the evidence that satisfies it. When a gate is up next (the one before it is done or ending) and has no evidence by its ask time, Sage posts ONE card for it: Booked / Book it for me / Not yet / Drop. Everything an organization tunes is here; the code only interprets it. Evidence sources: ledger (the delivery ledger), hb (the CRM snapshot), editor (the edit pipeline), calendar, followup, ticket, exec (what actually went out), chat (the owners' own words), register (assistant/data/registers/*.json), plus the owner's own tap on the gate's card, which always counts. default_amount: the dollars at stake for the priority brain when the record carries none (an average booking). question: the gate's own closing question (default 'Book it?').",
 "ask": {
  "_doc": "Defaults for every chain: a gate is asked from lead_days before its due date, re-asked after reask_days of silence, at most max_asks times; a chain may set offsets_days (days from the anchor, negative = before) and then asks only when the clock crosses an offset. ending_days: the previous gate counts as ending when its due date is within this many days. max_per_lane_per_day caps new chain cards per lane per day (the per-lane chaser is separate).",
  "lead_days": 7,
  "reask_days": 7,
  "max_asks": 3,
  "ending_days": 2,
  "max_per_lane_per_day": 2,
  "options": {
   "booked": "Booked",
   "book": "Book it for me",
   "not_yet": "Not yet",
   "drop": "Drop"
  }
 },
